WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.780
- If you're ashamed of who you are

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:05.850
and you're feeling like no
one else is gonna get me,

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.167
it's not true.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.750
(gentle music)

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.620
- I am a fully out lesbian woman

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.260
and I was raised in a
Jehovah's Witness household.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.090
- I grew up Roman Catholic
in Houston, Texas.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.820
Yes, the south and land of Beyonce.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.520
- I grew up in a religious household.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.160
It was very strict and unloving.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.520
- I grew up in an
Orthodox Jewish community.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.380
- I grew up in a Catholic household.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.550
- I got baptized when I
was a senior in high school

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.750
and then I ended up going to

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.790
a really conservative Christian college.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:45.220
- I grew up in a very
Catholic religious household.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.860
We're also part of the
Charismatic Renewal Group.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.120
So, we were even deeper into the church.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.290
- I realized really quickly
how the church viewed queerness

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.890
and it was not positive.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.250
- Just because this is
my Catholic experience

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.000
does not mean that every Catholic person

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.010
or every Catholic
experience was like this,

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.680
but for me in my small town,

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.210
the way that Catholicism was expressed

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.810
was very aggressively.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.657
- I would hear a lot of
sermons talking about

00:01:11.657 --> 00:01:14.740
"the lifestyle" that I am living

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.370
is deeming me to hell.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.500
So I kept it a secret for so long.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.040
- But one chaplain in particular,
the pastor is up there

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.540
saying that he took a trip
with his family to Puerto Rico,

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.920
and that he saw men holding hands together

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.110
and was wondering, "Why
did I pay all this money

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.670
to have to see something like that?

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:34.300
The atrocity. The sin."

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.630
And I remember sitting
there feeling so crappy

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.930
because essentially he
was talking about me.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.830
- There were lots of strict rules

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.783
and laws that we had to stick to.

00:01:43.783 --> 00:01:47.530
It made it very, very hard
to be able to express myself.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.420
- Most of the time,

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.700
I just felt like I was
a walking contradiction.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.870
I didn't identify with the
person that I was portraying

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.130
to the outside world.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:00.470
- I actually really
enjoyed singing in mass,

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:04.380
but then when it came down to being gay,

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.790
it wasn't something I felt accepted with.

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:12.230
- So one of my most
embarrassing and hurtful times

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.780
was when, I as the choir director,

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.360
one of the tenors are saying

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.867
in a nice beautiful tenor voice,

00:02:18.867 --> 00:02:20.767
"Reggie is a (beep)"

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:27.240
Nobody. Nobody stood up
and said a word for me.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.820
That was absolutely devastating.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:36.820
- I was taught that being
gay was plain old, wrong.

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.380
You know, you were going to hell.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.780
- I remember before I came out,

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.310
it felt like I had already
lost everybody in my life.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.620
- Growing up queer and black,

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.840
I really was just trying to survive.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.180
- So much of me was so scared

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:56.160
that my parents, that my
community, that my friends,

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.750
would no longer support me.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.780
- For the longest time, I
thought I was the only one.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.360
- There wasn't examples of someone like me

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.010
when I was growing up

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:07.540
that told me it was okay to be who I was.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.980
- Realizing that I was a
part of the LGBT community

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.900
was very empowering on one hand,

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.250
but on the other hand,
it was also very scary.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.630
- Every single week after I
came out that I went to church,

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.860
I would just pray that
the news hadn't spread.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.430
- I felt dirty.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.100
I didn't feel like I could be myself.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:25.513
- I felt ashamed of who I was at first.

00:03:25.513 --> 00:03:27.820
I felt very ashamed. I
tried to pray it away.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.140
- I left the church
when I was 16 years old

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:33.700
because I told my mother I
don't wanna come here anymore.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.447
I heard a lot of things about,

00:03:35.447 --> 00:03:37.720
"Don't do this, don't do that",

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.930
but I did not hear very much about love.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.540
And when I read the Bible,

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.470
I was seeing a lot of things about love.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.707
- And then I had a lot of
conversations with myself

00:03:46.707 --> 00:03:47.660
and with God.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.290
I just came to the conclusion

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.600
that it was okay to be who I was.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.750
- When I came out, I
lost most of my friends

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.770
and then I moved across the country

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.900
and made so many amazing friends

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.320
that loved me not despite who I was,

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.960
but because of who I was.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.340
- Once I went away out
of state for college,

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:10.700
I kind of allowed myself
to truly explore who I was.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:15.700
- In New York city, I could be
100% Reginald anywhere I am.

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:19.270
And if I can't be 100%
Reginald anywhere I am,

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.280
I don't go there.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.970
- It was a very long journey

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.660
to come to where I am with my parents now,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.890
but I think it's a great place.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:30.230
Is there still room to grow? Yes.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.510
But I think that where we're at

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.650
is a place that I never
thought we would be

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.384
even three years ago.

00:04:36.384 --> 00:04:39.820
- My relationship with my
mother has grown stronger.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.280
- I didn't come out to my mother

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.740
until actually I was 19 years old.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.070
She smiled and said, "Reginald,
I kind of thought so.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.910
But, I never taught you who to love.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.990
I just taught you to love.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.110
And no matter who you are or what you do,

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:00.140
you'll always be my son and
I will always love you."

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:02.640
- I've learned to love
myself because I deserve to.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.680
I deserve love.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:04.830
- I feel safer,

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.990
even in a world that is
still not safe for me.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.120
I still feel safer 'cause I know

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.540
that I'm living the life
that I want to live.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.500
- I think that I'm finally at a place

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:19.120
where I am 100% confident in my sexuality

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.590
and no part of me feels ashamed or hidden

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.080
or like a problem anymore.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.610
And if you are a person of faith

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.020
who does love and accept
all queer identities

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.530
and all people in general,

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:32.600
let that be known.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.350
- If you are an LGBTQ youth

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.800
that are living in an
intolerant environment,

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.490
I know that you probably
can't get away but know this,

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:45.670
you are completely loved and
you're completely lovable

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:49.490
just because you are enough.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.940
- If you are being made to feel

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:54.830
that your sexuality is inherently wrong,

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.760
that is a reflection of them and not you.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.030
- People are gonna make
you feel otherised,

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.530
sectioned off, like a sinner,

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:02.363
and you know what?

00:06:02.363 --> 00:06:03.920
That's not your problem.
That is now your problem.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.820
Your one job in this life
is to be authentic, period.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.450
- And if they don't love you,

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:11.480
there's a whole community of queer people

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:14.200
who will embrace you and
love you as their own.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.620
- You are not alone.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.930
- You are not alone.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.637
- I mean, I'm sitting right here.

00:06:18.637 --> 00:06:21.070
Do you see my queer body?
I'm literally right here.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:22.600
- You are not a sinner.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:24.270
- You are worthy of love.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.307
- There is a world out there
that wants to celebrate you.

00:06:26.307 --> 00:06:28.440
- You just got to find it.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.340
- I think God made me the exactly
the way I'm supposed to be

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:32.420
and that's the end of it.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:35.130
- And I'm a proud and out lesbian woman.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.450
God, it is like really great to say that.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:41.570
- Today, I can say I'm a proud, queer man,

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:46.570
who loves to gender bend
and explore his sexuality

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:51.620
in a way that I truly
never thought that I would.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:55.090
- My name is Reginald Thomas Brown.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.960
My pronouns are, they and them.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:02.960
I am a queer, gender
non-conforming, black revolutionary,

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:07.502
who is loving my life like it's gold.

00:07:07.502 --> 00:07:10.085
(bright music)

